data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"Let `step = size - overlap`. Window `j` covers words `[j * step, min(j * step + size, n))`, where\n`n` is the word count. Emit a window for each start that is inside the text. The loop must stop\nafter the window whose end is `n`, because any later window is contained in that one."},"hints_note":null}

